+- Build a task harness with explicit cases and scorer contracts.
+- Distinguish fixture/simulated scores from trained-model measurements.
+- Aggregate target NLL by scored-target count, excluding padding.
+- Freeze context, boundary, tail, and overlap policies.
+- Report failures and limits of small local experiments.
+
+## Python reference qualification
+
+**SIMULATED EVALUATION: fixture answers, heuristic judge, and model_quality-generated log probabilities are not measured trained-model performance. Excluded from model-quality claims.**
+
+For measured NLL, score each eligible target once under a common context policy. Sum target NLL and divide by actual scored-target count, never average unequal batch means. Declare document-start/BOS, EOS, final partial-window, context/stride, overlap deduplication, and padding exclusion. BPB divides total target NLL by ln(2) and the exact original UTF-8 content-byte count whose targets were scored, excluding inserted controls/padding. The mean_target_nll helper combines supplied totals; it does not measure a model. Its unequal-count test is (2 + 12)/(1 + 3) = 3.5, not 3.
+
+These boundaries qualify the reference; the incomplete/random/simulated routines have not been repaired into complete training or measurement.
 
